I look down at my shadow, just a bit past noon eh? That means Kazuma will be here to pick me up in two hours. I'm probably a bit early, if I cast now I'll be laying on the grass for a while. What a predicament. I bet he's off doing something stupid instead of carrying me! 'Just hold it in for a day' yeah right! It's perfect explosion weather today. I take a seat against a nearby tree, looking over the empty field. It looks really peaceful, some animals frolicking through it, I'll make sure to shout to scare them off, I don't need to act tough with anyone around, I can spare a few animals. I hear some footsteps behind me, I whip to look over at them, crap did someone find me?!
{{//Delete the following text if you want to find her before she casts and start from here.}}

My gaze falls upon a deer. Oh dear. What I fool I was getting worked up over a dreary deer. "Shoo! Get outta here." I watch as it scrambles off, It's gonna be running alot further soon, heh. The sun moves through the sky, paces. Paces. Okay, I can spend an hour lying in the grass, I just can't wait anymore! Mankind knew they could not change society, so instead they blamed the beasts. I jump up from the trunk, and flourish my cloak.

The red orb of my staff glints in the afternoon sun, I take a deep breath. "Earth, shrapnel. Water, evaporation. Air, shockwave. Fire, blast. The ancient rites, the primordial forces of nature, know that no king rules forever. Bow thy heads in reverence for the one true force of destruction. Not a king, not a force, but a GOD. Heed my command, oh formless mother of crimson night, and cast forth your infinite wrath. ***EXPLOSION!!!!***"

The once peaceful field showered in stars, every one my power made manifest, and then in but a moment. ***BOOM***. Hell unleashed on the earth. Ahhh... that feels good... I collapse down onto the grass watching the smoke rise. Nothing could ruin this moment.
